WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.574
The shortest route from Vietnam to Europe often goes through Singapore.

2
00:00:03.604 --> 00:00:08.641
Because mother ships, the giants that carry tens of thousands of boxes, need very deep water to berth.

3
00:00:08.671 --> 00:00:15.408
At a shallow port, cargo goes onto a small ship, sails to a transshipment hub, is unloaded, then loaded onto the mother ship again.

4
00:00:15.438 --> 00:00:20.135
Every extra handling means more fees, more days, and one more place to fall behind.

5
00:00:20.165 --> 00:00:23.851
Then Vietnam got a deep-water port cluster: Cái Mép – Thị Vải.

6
00:00:23.881 --> 00:00:30.584
In March 2023, a container ship almost four hundred metres long, able to carry more than twenty-four thousand TEU, docked here.

7
00:00:30.614 --> 00:00:37.789
By October 2024, twenty-two mother-ship services ran straight from here to the US and Europe, the most in Southeast Asia after Singapore.

8
00:00:37.819 --> 00:00:47.337
But even a deep port can jam. Ships wait for a berth, containers sit in the yard, and once free time runs out, every box pays storage fees every day, sometimes hundreds of dollars.

9
00:00:47.367 --> 00:00:56.522
Luckily, the bigger the ship, the cheaper the freight per box. Unluckily, the bigger the ship, the more boxes the port must move at once, and one slow beat leaves a mountain of cargo waiting.

10
00:00:56.552 --> 00:01:04.995
You see, a port is like a school gate at home time. A wide gate lets one big bus pick up the whole class. But jam the gate for ten minutes, and the whole bus gets home late.

11
00:01:05.025 --> 00:01:14.017
In Bật Nghiệp 3D, in round five, your team's cargo is stuck at Cái Mép. Pay a priority fee to deliver everything, wait to save money, or ask the customer for a later delivery date?

12
00:01:14.047 --> 00:01:19.147
A survey in Europe found that almost one in three shoppers trust a seller less after a single late delivery.

13
00:01:19.177 --> 00:01:25.705
A deep-water port saves cargo the long way round. But when the port jams, which way is shortest is for your team to choose.
